    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 081923 RRA\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1223 PM PDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n*  Above-normal temperatures expected mid-to-late week.\n\n*  Breezy south-southwesterly wind gusts expected across the region \n   Friday through the weekend.\n\n&&\n\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Monday.\nHigh pressure over the southern US will gradually expand and \nstrengthen over the Desert Southwest mid to late week. This will \nresult in rapidly warming temperatures Wednesday and Thursday with \ntemperatures climbing to around 8 to 10 degrees above normal. As a \nresult, an Extreme Heat Warning has been issued for Thursday for \nDeath Valley, the Las Vegas Valley, Pahrump Valley, Moapa Valley, \nColorado River Valley, southern Mohave County, and southeastern San \nBernardino County. Temperatures will begin to trend downward \nstarting Friday as a trough pushes into the western US. This will \nallow temperatures to drop about 5 degrees Friday along with an \nadditional drop around 2 to 4 degrees Saturday with temperatures \nclose to normal by early next week. Generally dry conditions are \nexpected, but some weak monsoonal moisture will be pulled northward \nWednesday and Thursday allowing for at least a slight chance of \nthunderstorms in the Sierra and terrain of the southern Great Basin \ndue to strong daytime heating and weak instability.\n\nThe aforementioned trough pushing into the western US will bring \ncooler temperatures but also bring increasing southwest winds to the \nregion. The strongest winds look to occur Saturday afternoon where \nwidespread gusts 25-35 MPH are expected, with over a 50% chance of \ngusts over 40 MPH in the western Mojave Desert. There could also be \nsome gusty southerly winds impacting Lake Mohave and Lake Havasu \nthis weekend, which could impact boaters with winds and waves. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Light \nwinds generally following typical diurnal directional trends will \ncontinue through the TAF period. Speeds will generally remain below \n8 knots, although a few gusts of 12 to 15 knots are possible during \nthe period of maximum heating this afternoon. VFR conditions will \nprevail through Tuesday with only a FEW to SCT mid- and high-level \nclouds at times. Temperatures should top out right around 100F by \nmid to late afternoon. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Favorable aviation \nconditions will persist across the region through Tuesday with winds \ngenerally following typical daily directional patterns and speeds \nremaining 12 knots or less. VFR conditions will prevail with only a \nFEW to SCT mid- and high-level clouds streaming across the region at \ntimes.  \n\n&&\n\nCLIMATE...Numerous climate locations have a forecast high\ntemperature and/or forecast warm low temperature within 3 degrees of \nthe daily record.\n\nThe table below shows the daily record maximum temperature and the \nyear the record was last set. An asterisk (*) denotes which records \nare in jeopardy (within 3 degrees of the forecast).\n\nMAX           WED, SEP 9  THU, SEP 10  FRI, SEP 11 \n              Record(Yr)  Record(Yr)   Record (Yr)\n \nLas Vegas     108(1944)   108(1945)*   109(1945) \nBishop        101(2022)   100(1993)*   101(2015) \nNeedles       113(2021)   113(1990)*   114(1990) \nDaggett       110(1993)   109(1993)    108(1979) \nKingman       107(1910)   103(1932)*   102(1937) \nDesert Rock   104(2021)*  103(1993)*   104(2015)* \nDeath Valley  120(1923)   119(2012)    119(1993)\n\nThe table below shows the daily record warm minimum temperature and \nthe year the record was last set. An asterisk (*) denotes which \nrecords are in jeopardy (within 3 degrees of the forecast).\n\nWARM MIN      WED, SEP 9  THU, SEP 10  FRI, SEP 11\n              Record(Yr)  Record(Yr)   Record (Yr)\n\nLas Vegas     85(2022)*   83(2021)*    81(2024)* \nBishop        60(1960)    62(2022)     62(1992) \nNeedles       88(1979)    87(2021)*    91(1969) \nDaggett       79(2024)*   81(1984)*    79(1971)* \nKingman       76(1914)    84(1914)     78(1914)* \nDesert Rock   74(2021)*   78(1994)*    75(2021)*\nDeath Valley  98(2021)    95(2012)*    93(2021)* \n\n&&\n\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Gorelow\nAVIATION...Planz\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
